wifi_meshmgr: check the dealloc result in if_create_sync error labels

nss_wifi_meshmgr_if_create_sync() unwinds its two dynamic-interface
allocations on five error labels. The dealloc return value is discarded
and the warn that follows guards nss_status, which has nothing to do with
the dealloc it claims to report:

	- on the encap_reg_fail, decap_alloc_fail and decap_reg_fail gotos,
	  nss_status has never been assigned, so the guard reads it
	  uninitialized;
	- on the config_failed path, nss_status holds the last config-message
	  status, so a config failure prints "Decap/Encap interface dealloc
	  failed: %d" carrying an unrelated status;
	- a genuine dealloc failure is never reported on any path.

nss_dynamic_interface_dealloc_node() returns nss_tx_status_t, not
nss_wifi_meshmgr_status_t, so the dealloc result cannot simply be stored
in nss_status without a type mismatch -- the guard tests the wrong
variable rather than being one assignment short.

Check each dealloc's own return against NSS_TX_SUCCESS and drop the
nss_status reads at the labels. nss_status is then only read where it was
just assigned (the config-message sends), so the declaration initializer
the previous version of this patch added is no longer load-bearing and is
gone.

The identical wrong-guard pattern is in pristine 11.4 and 12.5 and in
qosmio's shipped 11.4 tree; qosmio mutes the uninitialized read by
initializing nss_status at declaration, which this patch does not carry
forward. A sweep of the file found no other instance of this pattern.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

--- a/wifi_meshmgr/nss_wifi_meshmgr.c
+++ b/wifi_meshmgr/nss_wifi_meshmgr.c
@@ -1920,16 +1920,14 @@
 config_failed:
 	nss_unregister_wifi_mesh_if(decap_ifnum);
 decap_reg_fail:
-	nss_dynamic_interface_dealloc_node(decap_ifnum, NSS_DYNAMIC_INTERFACE_TYPE_WIFI_MESH_OUTER);
-	if (nss_status != NSS_WIFI_MESHMGR_SUCCESS) {
-		nss_wifi_meshmgr_warn("%px: Decap interface dealloc failed: %d\n", dev, nss_status);
+	if (nss_dynamic_interface_dealloc_node(decap_ifnum, NSS_DYNAMIC_INTERFACE_TYPE_WIFI_MESH_OUTER) != NSS_TX_SUCCESS) {
+		nss_wifi_meshmgr_warn("%px: Decap interface dealloc failed\n", dev);
 	}
 decap_alloc_fail:
 	nss_unregister_wifi_mesh_if(encap_ifnum);
 encap_reg_fail:
-	nss_dynamic_interface_dealloc_node(encap_ifnum, NSS_DYNAMIC_INTERFACE_TYPE_WIFI_MESH_INNER);
-	if (nss_status != NSS_WIFI_MESHMGR_SUCCESS) {
-		nss_wifi_meshmgr_warn("%px: Encap interface dealloc failed: %d\n", dev, nss_status);
+	if (nss_dynamic_interface_dealloc_node(encap_ifnum, NSS_DYNAMIC_INTERFACE_TYPE_WIFI_MESH_INNER) != NSS_TX_SUCCESS) {
+		nss_wifi_meshmgr_warn("%px: Encap interface dealloc failed\n", dev);
 	}
 encap_alloc_fail:
 	kfree(wmesh_ctx);
